The attention-weighted timing spectrum is defined as:

\begin{equation}
F(\omega) = \sum_k \alpha_k e^{-i\omega\Delta t_k}
\end{equation}

where $\alpha_k$ are attention weights and $\Delta t_k$ are token generation latencies.

The inverse discrete-time Fourier transform reveals:

\begin{equation}
\tilde{F}(t) = \frac{1}{2\pi} \int_{-\pi}^{\pi} F(\omega) e^{i\omega t} d\omega
